    {
      "title": "7 killed, 7 injured as landslide hits Mumbai's Ghatkopar after heavy rains",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/india-news/2-dead-several-feared-trapped-after-landslide-in-mumbai-s-ghatkopar-126081200358_1.html",
      "description": "Two persons were killed and six to eight others feared trapped after a landslide in Mumbai's Ghatkopar area early on Wednesday following heavy rain, civic officials said.\nThe civic body had earlier said the incident occurred in Kurla, a neighbouring area.\nThe landslide was reported at Gaushiya Chawl (row tenement) in Chirag Nagar at 3.48 am, the Brihanmumbai Municipal Corporation (BMC) officials said.\nSearch and rescue operations were underway, with teams of the fire brigade, police, NDRF, ambulance service and civic ward staff deployed at the site.\nTwo bodies have been recovered from the debris and sent to Rajawadi Hospital, as per BMC officials.\nTwo others, identified as Sohel Ansari (18), who suffered a head injury, and Mohamad Ansari, 14, who sustained a back injury, were undergoing treatment at the civic-run Bhabha Hospital in Kurla. Both were in stable condition, an official said.\nMumbai Mayor Ritu Tawde also reached the spot to supervise the search and rescue operations.",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-08-12T04:44:53"
    }
  ]
